        "text_faRqN3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The K-Swiss Ultrashot has built a reputation for stability, durability, and confidence-inspiring performance on court. With the release of Ultrashot 4, K-Swiss introduces new technologies designed to enhance control and support—while preserving the qualities players appreciated in Ultrashot 3. This guide breaks down what’s new, how the two versions compare, and which shoe may be the better fit for your game.</p><p></p><p><strong>What’s New in the K-Swiss Ultrashot - the 4th Generation</strong></p><p>Ultrashot 4 builds on its predecessor's foundation, focusing on improved stability and structure during aggressive play. Key updates include:</p><p>Shock Frame Technology: Designed to improve lateral stability and energy transfer, particularly during quick direction changes.</p><p>Carbon Winglet Technology: Adds targeted support to help keep the foot secure during high-intensity movement.</p><p>180-Day Outsole Warranty: Ultrashot 4 is built to last, and we’ll replace it if it breaks down in the first 180 days.</p><p>Vibrant new colorways: Performance-first design meets colors that pop.</p><p>These enhancements are aimed at players who play fast, move aggressively, and want extra confidence when pushing their limits on court.</p>"
          }
